window.CET4_BANKS.push({"id": "2025-12-3", "source": "2025年12月真题·第3套", "writing": {"prompt": "Directions: Suppose your university is organizing a forum on how students can make the best use of on-campus resources for academic development. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.", "sample": "On-campus resources are a treasure that too many students overlook. In my view, actively making use of these\nfacilities is one of the smartest ways to boost our academic development.\nThere are several practical steps we can take. First, we should visit the library and its online databases\nregularly, since they offer academic papers and books that turn a rough idea into a well-supported argument.\nMoreover, we ought to consult professors during their office hours, because a ten-minute talk often clears up\nconfusion that hours of self-study cannot. In addition, attending academic lectures and joining study groups\nexposes us to fresh perspectives and keeps our motivation high.\nIn short, the campus is full of tools waiting to be used. Only by taking the initiative to utilize them can we truly\ngrow as learners and get the most out of our university years."}, "translation": {"prompt": "中国政府十分重视绿色经济的发展。通过加强森林资源保护、加大污染治理力度等一系列措施，许多地区的生态环境得到了显著改善。绿水青山 (lucid waters and lush mountains) 促进了当地的旅游、健康等产业的发展，创造了可观的经济效益。如今，生态环境与人类社会和谐共存的观念在中国已深入人心。绿色经济的推进不仅能为中国可持续发展做出贡献，也为全球环境保护提供了宝贵经验。", "sample": "The Chinese government attaches great importance to the development of the green economy. Through a series of measures such as strengthening forest resource protection and intensifying pollution control, the ecological environment in many regions has improved remarkably. Lucid waters and lush mountains have promoted the development of local industries such as tourism and health care, generating considerable economic benefits. Today, the idea that ecology and human society can coexist in harmony has taken deep root in China. The promotion of the green economy not only contributes to China's sustainable development but also provides valuable experience for global environmental protection."}, "listeningUrl": null, "clozePassage": "Earth Day is an annual celebration that honors the achievements of the environmental movement and raises awareness of the need to protect Earth's natural resources for future generations. Earth Day is celebrated on April 22 in the United States and on either April 22 or the day the spring equinox(春分) occurs throughout the  __26__  of the world.\nEnvironmental activism during the 1960s  __27__  Wisconsin Senator Gaylord Nelson to create a  __28__  celebration uniting the environmental movement. With the help of Denis Hayes, a graduate student at Harvard University, Nelson organized the first Earth Day on April 22, 1970, educating participants in the  __29__  of environmental protection. Attended by 20 million people across the United States, the event  __30__  support for legislation such as the Clean Air Act and the Endangered Species Act.\nIn 1990, Hayes organized a global Earth Day, with more than 200 million participants in 140 countries. Earth Day now brings  __31__  citizens and activists from around the world to raise awareness and take action regarding such environmental  __32__  as global warming and renewable energy.\nToday, the Earth Day Network, which rallies more than 20,000  __33__  and organizations in 190 countries, supports the Earth Day mission year-round. This mission is founded on the proposition that all people, regardless of race, gender, income, or  __34__  , have a moral right to a healthy, sustainable environment. The Earth Day Network  __35__  this mission through education, public policy, and activism campaigns.", "matchIntro": "Looking for a job after 45", "matchParagraphs": [{"label": "A", "text": "Ageism and long-term unemployment are most damaging for those in the second half of their careers. Changing careers is hard. Getting back into work after you've been laid off is even harder. Those over 45 make up the bulk of the long-term unemployed, in America and elsewhere. Hiring managers admit they are reluctant to hire those over 40 or 45, arguing they probably won't be a good \"fit,\" their experience won't be relevant to the workplace, and they'll be unable or unwilling to learn new skills."}, {"label": "B", "text": "But the one thing that can really make a difference? More education and training. These are the results from a new study by Generation, a nonprofit founded by former McKinsey consultants. They've just published a global survey on midcareer employment, based on surveys of over 5,000 workers and managers in seven countries."}, {"label": "C", "text": "\"Older midcareer workers … make up the bulk of the long-term unemployed in many countries,\" Generation's analysts write in their report. Those over 45 comprise over 40% of the long-term unemployed, for example. And if you're out of work past the age of 45, there's nearly a two in three chance you'll be out of work for over a year, they find. \"Midcareer individuals are finding it harder to get jobs,\" they write. \"People age 45+ face persistent and rising pressure in the global job market. They are unemployed for much longer than the average, and their age is indeed one of the greatest barriers to their finding a job.\""}, {"label": "D", "text": "A substantial part of this, they report, is \"widespread ageism\" on the part of hiring managers. Although such managers admit that post-45 hires turn out on average to be just as good as or better than younger workers, they still don't want to hire them. \"Hiring managers have a strong perception bias against 45+ job candidates — they believe that members of this age group have poor skills and low adaptability,\" Generation's analysts report."}, {"label": "E", "text": "The survey results are remarkable. Hiring managers are three times as likely to rate job applicants age 35 – 44 as a better \"fit\" than those over 45. They rate the post-45 job seekers lower on average on all three measures — even experience — than those ages 18 to 34. This is true even though nearly nine managers in 10 also said their post-45 workers were as good as or better than younger employees in the same jobs."}, {"label": "F", "text": "Their biggest fears about hiring those over 45? Managers said they worry that older hires will be reluctant to try new technologies, and will be unable to learn new skills. Besides, the majority of hiring managers are under 45 — and seem reluctant to hire people older than themselves."}, {"label": "G", "text": "But here's the good news. Older workers who've actively engaged in more education and training relevant to their jobs turn this pretty much on its head. Three-quarters of hiring managers said they'd be more likely to hire an over-45 who had relevant education, training or credentials(文凭). Among those over 45 who'd successfully switched careers, 74% said training helped them get their new job."}, {"label": "H", "text": "\"Midcareer switchers overwhelmingly say that training enabled them to shift to a new career path,\" the analysts write. And when they asked over-45 candidates about their attitudes, they found that \"those who are excited by training are unemployed for less time, receive more job offers, and are more satisfied by the job offers they receive.\""}, {"label": "I", "text": "Hiring managers said training was three times more likely to get them to hire applicants over age 45 than, say, government subsidies(补贴). What training are we talking about? Obviously it depends on the job. And, yes, managers are most likely to be impressed by industry qualifications you get in school. These things cost money, and time. But these aren't the only things helpful. Those who had successfully changed careers after 45 told Generation that education and training had been a big help — and that included in-person, on-the-job training, \"informal learning,\" and online courses — with or without certification."}, {"label": "J", "text": "If they think we're too old to learn new skills after we're 45, just learning some new skills may have an effect on its own. There's a downside to this. The people least interested in retraining are more likely to come from historically disadvantaged communities, more likely to have low incomes, and are more likely to have the least schooling after getting their high-school diploma or earlier. On average, post-45 job switchers with higher incomes participate in 2.5 training programs each. Those with lower incomes: 0.9 programs on average."}, {"label": "K", "text": "Many years ago, I wrote about a study which found that employers are much more likely to hire a college graduate who has some work experience in the industry than a college graduate who took the \"right\" degree. A bank is more likely to hire a literature graduate who spent their summers working in their local bank than a finance or economics graduate who spent their summers surfing or traveling around Italy. They've learned through long experience. The person who worked in the bank is more likely ready, willing and able to be part of the team and do the job from day 1."}, {"label": "L", "text": "We can rail against \"ageism\" all we like. It gets us nowhere. And it's easy to forget that employers, like everyone else, are under time pressure and are just trying to solve problems. Any and all \"training,\" including inexpensive and informal training, is going to help resolve their worries about hiring someone over 45. And it has never been easier or cheaper to gain instruction in new skills, thanks to the internet. Online schools like Udemy and Lynda.com offer sweet deals at sign-up. And courses on YouTube are free."}, {"label": "M", "text": "Bottom line? Yes, it really can be difficult getting a new job after age 45, let alone changing careers. One of the best things we can do to help ourselves is to go online and learn new, relevant skills. Sadly, the people who most need the help are least likely to take it — which raises a challenge for society as a whole. Not only do we not want to see lives go to waste, but we all benefit if more people are working and fewer are unemployed."}], "readingPassages": {"46": "New York's Eleven Madison Park has become the first vegan(素食主义的) restaurant to be awarded three Michelin stars.\nThe fine dining establishment received its first three-star Michelin rating in 2011 when the menu was famed for its fancy animal-based dishes.\nHowever, last year, the restaurant's co-owner and famous chef, Daniel Humm, made the bold decision to remove meat from the menu, citing our unsustainable food system. While cow milk is still served for tea and coffee, the menu is almost 100 percent vegan.\nAt the time, Humm acknowledged the move was risky, admitting that \"it wasn't clear if guests would come\", but called the gamble \"a risk worth taking.\"\n\"In view of the climate crisis, I didn't want to open the same restaurant,\" Humm told the Financial Times in an interview. \"If we can show the possibilities of eating plant-based food in this setting, it can open a lot of doors\" for others to follow.\nNow, this impressive new accomplishment validates Eleven Madison Park's decision to take meat off the menu and embrace plant-based foods, with Michelin's 2022 New York guide branding it 'a bold vision of luxury dining'.\n\"We took the jump to transform Eleven Madison Park into a plant-based fine dining restaurant knowing in our hearts this is what we believed in,\" stated Humm on Instagram. \"Last night, we were honored to be awarded three Michelin stars for the 11th year in a row. I am so grateful to the team members who contributed through its nearly 25-year history. We are also grateful to our guests and partners who believed in our vision and encouraged us to push harder.\"\nThree Michelin stars is the highest award, given to chefs who are at the peak of their profession. \"Their cooking is elevated to an art form and some of their dishes are destined to become classics,\" reads Michelin's website, in a clear nod to plant-based foods' growing significance in the culinary(烹饪的) world.\n\"I think luxury companies have a real role to play and a responsibility,\" says Humm. \"The more creative we are, the more beautiful and delicious our future will be.\"", "47": "New York's Eleven Madison Park has become the first vegan(素食主义的) restaurant to be awarded three Michelin stars.\nThe fine dining establishment received its first three-star Michelin rating in 2011 when the menu was famed for its fancy animal-based dishes.\nHowever, last year, the restaurant's co-owner and famous chef, Daniel Humm, made the bold decision to remove meat from the menu, citing our unsustainable food system. While cow milk is still served for tea and coffee, the menu is almost 100 percent vegan.\nAt the time, Humm acknowledged the move was risky, admitting that \"it wasn't clear if guests would come\", but called the gamble \"a risk worth taking.\"\n\"In view of the climate crisis, I didn't want to open the same restaurant,\" Humm told the Financial Times in an interview. \"If we can show the possibilities of eating plant-based food in this setting, it can open a lot of doors\" for others to follow.\nNow, this impressive new accomplishment validates Eleven Madison Park's decision to take meat off the menu and embrace plant-based foods, with Michelin's 2022 New York guide branding it 'a bold vision of luxury dining'.\n\"We took the jump to transform Eleven Madison Park into a plant-based fine dining restaurant knowing in our hearts this is what we believed in,\" stated Humm on Instagram. \"Last night, we were honored to be awarded three Michelin stars for the 11th year in a row. I am so grateful to the team members who contributed through its nearly 25-year history. We are also grateful to our guests and partners who believed in our vision and encouraged us to push harder.\"\nThree Michelin stars is the highest award, given to chefs who are at the peak of their profession. \"Their cooking is elevated to an art form and some of their dishes are destined to become classics,\" reads Michelin's website, in a clear nod to plant-based foods' growing significance in the culinary(烹饪的) world.\n\"I think luxury companies have a real role to play and a responsibility,\" says Humm. \"The more creative we are, the more beautiful and delicious our future will be.\"", "48": "New York's Eleven Madison Park has become the first vegan(素食主义的) restaurant to be awarded three Michelin stars.\nThe fine dining establishment received its first three-star Michelin rating in 2011 when the menu was famed for its fancy animal-based dishes.\nHowever, last year, the restaurant's co-owner and famous chef, Daniel Humm, made the bold decision to remove meat from the menu, citing our unsustainable food system. While cow milk is still served for tea and coffee, the menu is almost 100 percent vegan.\nAt the time, Humm acknowledged the move was risky, admitting that \"it wasn't clear if guests would come\", but called the gamble \"a risk worth taking.\"\n\"In view of the climate crisis, I didn't want to open the same restaurant,\" Humm told the Financial Times in an interview. \"If we can show the possibilities of eating plant-based food in this setting, it can open a lot of doors\" for others to follow.\nNow, this impressive new accomplishment validates Eleven Madison Park's decision to take meat off the menu and embrace plant-based foods, with Michelin's 2022 New York guide branding it 'a bold vision of luxury dining'.\n\"We took the jump to transform Eleven Madison Park into a plant-based fine dining restaurant knowing in our hearts this is what we believed in,\" stated Humm on Instagram. \"Last night, we were honored to be awarded three Michelin stars for the 11th year in a row. I am so grateful to the team members who contributed through its nearly 25-year history. We are also grateful to our guests and partners who believed in our vision and encouraged us to push harder.\"\nThree Michelin stars is the highest award, given to chefs who are at the peak of their profession. \"Their cooking is elevated to an art form and some of their dishes are destined to become classics,\" reads Michelin's website, in a clear nod to plant-based foods' growing significance in the culinary(烹饪的) world.\n\"I think luxury companies have a real role to play and a responsibility,\" says Humm. \"The more creative we are, the more beautiful and delicious our future will be.\"", "49": "New York's Eleven Madison Park has become the first vegan(素食主义的) restaurant to be awarded three Michelin stars.\nThe fine dining establishment received its first three-star Michelin rating in 2011 when the menu was famed for its fancy animal-based dishes.\nHowever, last year, the restaurant's co-owner and famous chef, Daniel Humm, made the bold decision to remove meat from the menu, citing our unsustainable food system. While cow milk is still served for tea and coffee, the menu is almost 100 percent vegan.\nAt the time, Humm acknowledged the move was risky, admitting that \"it wasn't clear if guests would come\", but called the gamble \"a risk worth taking.\"\n\"In view of the climate crisis, I didn't want to open the same restaurant,\" Humm told the Financial Times in an interview. \"If we can show the possibilities of eating plant-based food in this setting, it can open a lot of doors\" for others to follow.\nNow, this impressive new accomplishment validates Eleven Madison Park's decision to take meat off the menu and embrace plant-based foods, with Michelin's 2022 New York guide branding it 'a bold vision of luxury dining'.\n\"We took the jump to transform Eleven Madison Park into a plant-based fine dining restaurant knowing in our hearts this is what we believed in,\" stated Humm on Instagram. \"Last night, we were honored to be awarded three Michelin stars for the 11th year in a row. I am so grateful to the team members who contributed through its nearly 25-year history. We are also grateful to our guests and partners who believed in our vision and encouraged us to push harder.\"\nThree Michelin stars is the highest award, given to chefs who are at the peak of their profession. \"Their cooking is elevated to an art form and some of their dishes are destined to become classics,\" reads Michelin's website, in a clear nod to plant-based foods' growing significance in the culinary(烹饪的) world.\n\"I think luxury companies have a real role to play and a responsibility,\" says Humm. \"The more creative we are, the more beautiful and delicious our future will be.\"", "50": "New York's Eleven Madison Park has become the first vegan(素食主义的) restaurant to be awarded three Michelin stars.\nThe fine dining establishment received its first three-star Michelin rating in 2011 when the menu was famed for its fancy animal-based dishes.\nHowever, last year, the restaurant's co-owner and famous chef, Daniel Humm, made the bold decision to remove meat from the menu, citing our unsustainable food system. While cow milk is still served for tea and coffee, the menu is almost 100 percent vegan.\nAt the time, Humm acknowledged the move was risky, admitting that \"it wasn't clear if guests would come\", but called the gamble \"a risk worth taking.\"\n\"In view of the climate crisis, I didn't want to open the same restaurant,\" Humm told the Financial Times in an interview. \"If we can show the possibilities of eating plant-based food in this setting, it can open a lot of doors\" for others to follow.\nNow, this impressive new accomplishment validates Eleven Madison Park's decision to take meat off the menu and embrace plant-based foods, with Michelin's 2022 New York guide branding it 'a bold vision of luxury dining'.\n\"We took the jump to transform Eleven Madison Park into a plant-based fine dining restaurant knowing in our hearts this is what we believed in,\" stated Humm on Instagram. \"Last night, we were honored to be awarded three Michelin stars for the 11th year in a row. I am so grateful to the team members who contributed through its nearly 25-year history. We are also grateful to our guests and partners who believed in our vision and encouraged us to push harder.\"\nThree Michelin stars is the highest award, given to chefs who are at the peak of their profession. \"Their cooking is elevated to an art form and some of their dishes are destined to become classics,\" reads Michelin's website, in a clear nod to plant-based foods' growing significance in the culinary(烹饪的) world.\n\"I think luxury companies have a real role to play and a responsibility,\" says Humm. \"The more creative we are, the more beautiful and delicious our future will be.\"", "51": "With genetic testing becoming increasingly popular, many people are left wondering exactly how accurate it is. Whether you are taking a DNA test to build your extended DNA family tree, or want precise information on inborn(先天的) health conditions, it is important to understand how accurate genetic tests are, and what information we can rely upon.\nHow accurate DNA tests are relies greatly upon the kind of test being taken, on the specific question you ask, and on how complex the genetics behind a trait(特征) is. For example, tests for traits that depend on a single gene provide much more reliable results, because you can see whether a disease-causing trait is present.\nAncestry tests claim to reveal our genetic identities. But saying you are 30 percent East Asian or American hardly reflects your real ancestry.\nWhat about using DNA tests to discover distant family members? There are tools to compare one's DNA with others' to find distant relatives based on their genetic identification. These kinds of applications are generally accurate. It's relatively easy to tell whether two DNA samples belong to close relatives. With distant relatives, results become hazier.\nGenetic health tests claim to be able to detect certain hereditary(遗传的) diseases, or other health conditions. While certain rare diseases can be easily identified, most potential health conditions cannot be identified by genetic testing alone. The large majority of our traits and diseases also depend upon non-genetic factors, such as lifestyle, the environment, and many others.\nGenetic tests for multi-factorial traits are often very tricky to interpret. Height, for example, depends on hundreds of genes, each contributing a little to the outcome, together with a bunch of environmental factors. A test can look at many genes at once, but it's difficult to predict how they will play together. Then you should also account for non-genetic factors that are not written in the DNA.\nTests that offer to find your perfect romantic match and those claiming to predict personality or talents based on your DNA are pure nonsense. At the moment, the scientific bases for these applications are non-existent or incredibly weak.", "52": "With genetic testing becoming increasingly popular, many people are left wondering exactly how accurate it is. Whether you are taking a DNA test to build your extended DNA family tree, or want precise information on inborn(先天的) health conditions, it is important to understand how accurate genetic tests are, and what information we can rely upon.\nHow accurate DNA tests are relies greatly upon the kind of test being taken, on the specific question you ask, and on how complex the genetics behind a trait(特征) is. For example, tests for traits that depend on a single gene provide much more reliable results, because you can see whether a disease-causing trait is present.\nAncestry tests claim to reveal our genetic identities. But saying you are 30 percent East Asian or American hardly reflects your real ancestry.\nWhat about using DNA tests to discover distant family members? There are tools to compare one's DNA with others' to find distant relatives based on their genetic identification. These kinds of applications are generally accurate. It's relatively easy to tell whether two DNA samples belong to close relatives. With distant relatives, results become hazier.\nGenetic health tests claim to be able to detect certain hereditary(遗传的) diseases, or other health conditions. While certain rare diseases can be easily identified, most potential health conditions cannot be identified by genetic testing alone. The large majority of our traits and diseases also depend upon non-genetic factors, such as lifestyle, the environment, and many others.\nGenetic tests for multi-factorial traits are often very tricky to interpret. Height, for example, depends on hundreds of genes, each contributing a little to the outcome, together with a bunch of environmental factors. A test can look at many genes at once, but it's difficult to predict how they will play together. Then you should also account for non-genetic factors that are not written in the DNA.\nTests that offer to find your perfect romantic match and those claiming to predict personality or talents based on your DNA are pure nonsense. At the moment, the scientific bases for these applications are non-existent or incredibly weak.", "53": "With genetic testing becoming increasingly popular, many people are left wondering exactly how accurate it is. Whether you are taking a DNA test to build your extended DNA family tree, or want precise information on inborn(先天的) health conditions, it is important to understand how accurate genetic tests are, and what information we can rely upon.\nHow accurate DNA tests are relies greatly upon the kind of test being taken, on the specific question you ask, and on how complex the genetics behind a trait(特征) is. For example, tests for traits that depend on a single gene provide much more reliable results, because you can see whether a disease-causing trait is present.\nAncestry tests claim to reveal our genetic identities. But saying you are 30 percent East Asian or American hardly reflects your real ancestry.\nWhat about using DNA tests to discover distant family members? There are tools to compare one's DNA with others' to find distant relatives based on their genetic identification. These kinds of applications are generally accurate. It's relatively easy to tell whether two DNA samples belong to close relatives. With distant relatives, results become hazier.\nGenetic health tests claim to be able to detect certain hereditary(遗传的) diseases, or other health conditions. While certain rare diseases can be easily identified, most potential health conditions cannot be identified by genetic testing alone. The large majority of our traits and diseases also depend upon non-genetic factors, such as lifestyle, the environment, and many others.\nGenetic tests for multi-factorial traits are often very tricky to interpret. Height, for example, depends on hundreds of genes, each contributing a little to the outcome, together with a bunch of environmental factors. A test can look at many genes at once, but it's difficult to predict how they will play together. Then you should also account for non-genetic factors that are not written in the DNA.\nTests that offer to find your perfect romantic match and those claiming to predict personality or talents based on your DNA are pure nonsense. At the moment, the scientific bases for these applications are non-existent or incredibly weak.", "54": "With genetic testing becoming increasingly popular, many people are left wondering exactly how accurate it is. Whether you are taking a DNA test to build your extended DNA family tree, or want precise information on inborn(先天的) health conditions, it is important to understand how accurate genetic tests are, and what information we can rely upon.\nHow accurate DNA tests are relies greatly upon the kind of test being taken, on the specific question you ask, and on how complex the genetics behind a trait(特征) is. For example, tests for traits that depend on a single gene provide much more reliable results, because you can see whether a disease-causing trait is present.\nAncestry tests claim to reveal our genetic identities. But saying you are 30 percent East Asian or American hardly reflects your real ancestry.\nWhat about using DNA tests to discover distant family members? There are tools to compare one's DNA with others' to find distant relatives based on their genetic identification. These kinds of applications are generally accurate. It's relatively easy to tell whether two DNA samples belong to close relatives. With distant relatives, results become hazier.\nGenetic health tests claim to be able to detect certain hereditary(遗传的) diseases, or other health conditions. While certain rare diseases can be easily identified, most potential health conditions cannot be identified by genetic testing alone. The large majority of our traits and diseases also depend upon non-genetic factors, such as lifestyle, the environment, and many others.\nGenetic tests for multi-factorial traits are often very tricky to interpret. Height, for example, depends on hundreds of genes, each contributing a little to the outcome, together with a bunch of environmental factors. A test can look at many genes at once, but it's difficult to predict how they will play together. Then you should also account for non-genetic factors that are not written in the DNA.\nTests that offer to find your perfect romantic match and those claiming to predict personality or talents based on your DNA are pure nonsense. At the moment, the scientific bases for these applications are non-existent or incredibly weak.", "55": "With genetic testing becoming increasingly popular, many people are left wondering exactly how accurate it is. Whether you are taking a DNA test to build your extended DNA family tree, or want precise information on inborn(先天的) health conditions, it is important to understand how accurate genetic tests are, and what information we can rely upon.\nHow accurate DNA tests are relies greatly upon the kind of test being taken, on the specific question you ask, and on how complex the genetics behind a trait(特征) is. For example, tests for traits that depend on a single gene provide much more reliable results, because you can see whether a disease-causing trait is present.\nAncestry tests claim to reveal our genetic identities. But saying you are 30 percent East Asian or American hardly reflects your real ancestry.\nWhat about using DNA tests to discover distant family members? There are tools to compare one's DNA with others' to find distant relatives based on their genetic identification. These kinds of applications are generally accurate. It's relatively easy to tell whether two DNA samples belong to close relatives. With distant relatives, results become hazier.\nGenetic health tests claim to be able to detect certain hereditary(遗传的) diseases, or other health conditions. While certain rare diseases can be easily identified, most potential health conditions cannot be identified by genetic testing alone. The large majority of our traits and diseases also depend upon non-genetic factors, such as lifestyle, the environment, and many others.\nGenetic tests for multi-factorial traits are often very tricky to interpret. Height, for example, depends on hundreds of genes, each contributing a little to the outcome, together with a bunch of environmental factors. A test can look at many genes at once, but it's difficult to predict how they will play together. Then you should also account for non-genetic factors that are not written in the DNA.\nTests that offer to find your perfect romantic match and those claiming to predict personality or talents based on your DNA are pure nonsense. At the moment, the scientific bases for these applications are non-existent or incredibly weak."}, "questions": [{"id": "2025-12-3-c-26", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 26, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "M", "analysis": "【答案】M) rest\n名词\n【词性槽】the ___ of the world：定冠词 + 空 + of，典型名词位\n【依据】the rest of the world：固定搭配，指\"世界其余地方\"\n本句对比的是\"美国（the United States）\"和\"世界其他地方\"两部分——Earth Day is\ncelebrated on April 22 in the United States and on either April 22 or the day the\nspring equinox(春分) occurs throughout the __(26)__ of the world. \"the rest of the\nworld\"（世界其余地方）正是这种二分对照的固定表达，语义和搭配双双吻合。\n【竞争词】A) concerns concerns of the world 语义错位\nconcerns 意为\"关切事项\"，\"the concerns of the world\"指\"世界的关切问题\"，与本句\"在世界\n其余地方庆祝\"的地理范围语义完全不搭。\nB) expansion expansion 指\"扩张\"，与对比语境不合\nthe expansion of the world 意为\"世界的扩张\"，原文要表达的是\"美国 vs 世界其他地方\"的地\n域对比，扩张没有对照含义，不通。\nD) geography geography 偏\"地理学/地形\"，不指\"其余地区\"\nthe geography of the world 通常指\"世界的地理（地形地貌）\"，强调地理特征，无法承担\"美\n国以外的其他地方\"这层\"其余\"含义。\nE) importance importance 是抽象\"重要性\"，与地点状语冲突\nthe importance of the world 意为\"世界的重要性\"，但本句是 throughout 引导的地点范围状\n语，需要的是\"地方\"概念，importance 完全跑题。\nI) partners partners 复数指\"合作伙伴们\"，与 the…of the world 不搭\nthe partners of the world 不是一个自然搭配，且 throughout \"遍及\"后接的是地理范围、不是\n人群。\nJ) potential potential 指\"潜力\"，不能承载\"地方\"语义\nthe potential of the world 意为\"世界的潜力\"，与 throughout 表达\"在……各地\"的地点范围意\n义不一致。\nL) rescues rescues 指\"救援\"，与本句话题彻底无关\nthe rescues of the world\"世界的救援\"在本句完全无依据，地球日叙述中并未涉及救援行动。", "points": ["选词填空", "名词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-27", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 27, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "G", "analysis": "【答案】G) inspired\n动词\n【词性槽】Environmental activism … ___ Wisconsin Senator … to create：主语后缺谓语，需谓\n语动词\n【依据】inspire sb to do sth：激励某人去做某事\nEnvironmental activism during the 1960s __(27)__ Wisconsin Senator Gaylord Nelson\nto create a national celebration uniting the environmental movement.——\"20 世纪\n60 年代的环保运动激励参议员去创立一场全国性的环保庆典\"，inspire sb to do 是英语里\n表\"激发某人做某事\"的高频固定搭配，过去式 inspired 也与下文 1970 年时间线一致。\n【竞争词】F) imposed impose 不能直接跟 sb to do 结构\nimpose 意为\"强加（义务/税收/规定）\"，典型结构是 impose sth on sb，无法直接构成\nimposed sb to do；语义上也偏\"强迫\"，与\"环保运动激励议员\"的正面叙述色彩相反。\nK) pursues pursues 时态错 + 搭配错\npursues 是一般现在时第三人称单数，本句叙述 1960 年代的过去事件，时态不匹配；且\npursue 后通常接\"目标/事业\"等宾语，不接\"sb to do\"。\n【易错】最具迷惑性的错误词是 F) —— imposed 时态对但结构错。Environmental activism\nduring the 1960s __(27)__ Wisconsin Senator Gaylord Nelson to create 极易因\nimposed 与 inspired 都是过去式而二选一卡壳；防坑要诀：impose 不接 sb to do（典\n型是 impose sth on sb），inspire 才有 inspire sb to do sth 的固定结构——记住搭配是\n关键。", "points": ["选词填空", "动词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-28", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 28, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "H", "analysis": "【答案】H) national\n形容词\n【词性槽】a ___ celebration：冠词 + 空 + 名词，定语位\n【依据】a national celebration：呼应\"全国统一的环保运动\"\n下文 With the help of Denis Hayes, a graduate student at Harvard University, Nelson\norganized the first Earth Day on April 22, 1970 和 Attended by 20 million people\nacross the United States 都明示这是一场\"全美\"的活动；\"a national celebration uniting\nthe environmental movement\"意为\"一场全国性的、把环保运动联合起来的庆典\"，与下\n文 20 million people across the United States 完全呼应。\n【竞争词】G) inspired inspired 修饰 celebration 语义牵强\nan inspired celebration 字面是\"一场受启发的庆典\"，inspired 通常修饰人或想法（an\ninspired idea/leader），用来修饰 celebration 极不自然，且与下文\"团结环保运动\"的目的没\n关联。\nJ) potential potential celebration 矛盾——既然 create 了就不再是\"潜在的\"\npotential 意为\"潜在的、可能的\"，但本句动词是 create（创立），创立出来的就是真实存在的\n庆典，不再是\"潜在\"。逻辑上自相矛盾。", "points": ["选词填空", "形容词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-29", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 29, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "E", "analysis": "【答案】E) importance\n名词\n【词性槽】in the ___ of：固定名词框架\n【依据】educate sb in the importance of sth：教育某人意识到某事的重要性\n原文语境：educating participants in the __(29)__ of environmental protection.——\"教\n育参与者认识到环保的重要性\"是地球日活动最朴素直接的目的。\"the importance of + 抽\n象名词\"也是英语高频搭配。\n【竞争词】A) concerns concerns 偏\"具体关切事项\"，搭配上 the + 单数感不对\nthe concern of environmental protection 即便存在也偏\"环保的关切对象\"，把它代回原句\"教\n育参与者认识环保的 concerns\"很别扭；且 concerns 是复数，与 the…of 单数框架的常见用法\n不顺。\nB) expansion expansion of environmental protection 在本句逻辑里突兀\nexpansion\"扩张\"代回得到\"教育参与者认识环保的扩张\"，本段并未涉及\"环保的扩张\"这一话\n题，与下文 support for legislation 的衔接也不顺。\nD) geography geography of environmental protection 不通\n\"环保的地理\"在本句毫无依据，且 educate sb in the geography of… 是\"教某人……的地理知\n识\"，与\"提高环保意识\"主旨完全不搭。\nI) partners partners 是复数且语义不对\nthe partners of environmental protection\"环保的合作伙伴\"既不符合\"教育参与者意识到\"的搭\n配，也与 33 题真正需要 partners 的位置冲突——本空若提前用掉 partners，后面 33 题就会\n卡壳。\nJ) potential potential of environmental protection 偏\"潜力\"，与下文不接\n\"环保的潜力\"语义上能讲通，但下文 the event __(30)__ support for legislation 落点是\"推动立\n法\"，靠的是参与者\"认识到环保的重要性\"才会去支持立法，而不是\"认识到环保的潜力\"。\nimportance 与下文因果衔接更紧。\nL) rescues rescues 完全跑题\n\"环保的救援\"于本句无任何上下文支持，是明显错项。\n【易错】最具迷惑性的错误词是 J) —— potential 沾边但抓不准因果。educating participants in\nthe __(29)__ of environmental protection 极易因为\"the potential of\"也是地道搭配而误\n选 J；防坑要诀：往下读一句，看下文落点是\"推动立法\"——要让人去推动立法，必须先认\n识到事情的\"重要性\"（importance）而不是\"潜力\"，因果链才接得上。", "points": ["选词填空", "名词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-30", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 30, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "N", "analysis": "【答案】N) strengthened\n动词\n【词性槽】the event ___ support：主语后缺谓语，需过去时动词\n【依据】strengthened support for legislation：增强了对立法的支持\nthe event __(30)__ support for legislation such as the Clean Air Act and the\nEndangered Species Act.——一场 2000 万人参与的环保活动，推动并加强了对清洁空气\n法案等环保立法的支持，这是因果链最自然的写法；strengthen support 是英语里高频积\n极搭配。\n【竞争词】F) imposed imposed support 搭配不成立、语义对抗\nimpose 意为\"强加\"，imposed support 字面是\"强加支持\"，搭配上极怪；且 impose 的对象常\n是 obligation/tax/sanction，用在公众自发推动立法这一正面语境里，色彩完全相反。", "points": ["选词填空", "动词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-31", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 31, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "O", "analysis": "【答案】O) together\n副词\n【词性槽】brings ___ citizens：bring 后接副词，构成 bring together 短语\n【依据】bring together：把（来自世界各地的人）聚到一起\nEarth Day now brings __(31)__ citizens and activists from around the world to raise\nawareness and take action——bring together citizens and activists from around the\nworld 是\"把全世界的公民和活动家聚到一起\"的标准表达，与下文\"共同提高意识、采取行\n动\"的语义完美衔接。\n【竞争词】C) forth bring forth 意为\"产生、提出\"，与\"人\"不搭\nbring forth 多用于 bring forth ideas/results/a child（产生想法/结果/孩子），后接\"人\"作宾\n语极不自然；且与下文\"从世界各地聚来\"的范围语义不符。", "points": ["选词填空", "副词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-32", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 32, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A) concerns\n名词\n【词性槽】such environmental ___ as global warming and renewable energy：such…as 结构里\n的复数名词\n【依据】environmental concerns：环境关切/环保议题\nsuch environmental __(32)__ as global warming and renewable energy——\"诸如全球\n变暖、可再生能源等环境议题\"，environmental concerns 是英语里描述环保领域议题最高\n频的固定搭配，与所举两例（一个问题、一个解决方向）都吻合。", "points": ["选词填空", "名词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-33", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 33, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "I", "analysis": "【答案】I) partners\n名词\n【词性槽】rallies more than 20,000 ___ and organizations：数量词+空+and+名词，并列名词位\n【依据】partners and organizations：\"合作伙伴 + 组织\"是地球日网络的天然描述\nthe Earth Day Network, which rallies more than 20,000 __(33)__ and organizations in\n190 countries——一个推动全球环保使命的网络，团结的正是各种 \"partners（合作伙伴/\n成员单位）和 organizations（组织）\"，这是英文里描述全球性平台最常见的表达。\n【竞争词】L) rescues rescues 不能和 organizations 并列指主体\nrescues\"救援行动\"是事件名词，无法与 organizations\"组织\"并列充当 rally（团结、聚集）的宾\n语——团结的对象应是\"人/单位\"，不是\"行动\"。语义错位。", "points": ["选词填空", "名词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-34", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 34, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D) geography\n名词\n【词性槽】race, gender, income, or ___：并列名词序列的末项\n【依据】geography 在此指\"地域/地区\"，与种族、性别、收入并列为人的归属属性\nall people, regardless of race, gender, income, or __(34)__, have a moral right to a\nhealthy, sustainable environment.——种族、性别、收入都是描述\"人是谁\"的范畴，\ngeography 用作\"地理（出身/所在地）\"恰好补全这一系列，强调\"无论你来自哪里\"。这种\n用法在英语严肃文体里常见，例如 regardless of geography\"不论地域\"。\n【竞争词】B) expansion expansion 不属于\"人的属性\"\nexpansion\"扩张\"不是描述人群差异的范畴，无法与 race/gender/income 同类并列。\nJ) potential potential 抽象但不属\"出身/分类\"维度\npotential\"潜力\"是个体能力描述，不是天然属性，逻辑上\"不论潜力如何\"在本句价值宣言中也不\n合常理——本句强调的是\"不论出身条件\"，而非\"不论能力高低\"。", "points": ["选词填空", "名词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-c-35", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 35, "stem": "", "options": ["A) concerns", "B) expansion", "C) forth", "D) geography", "E) importance", "F) imposed", "G) inspired", "H) national", "I) partners", "J) potential", "K) pursues", "L) rescues", "M) rest", "N) strengthened", "O) together"], "answer": "K", "analysis": "【答案】K) pursues\n动词\n【词性槽】The Earth Day Network ___ this mission：主语后缺谓语，需第三人称单数现在时动词\n【依据】pursues this mission：推行/践行这一使命\nThe Earth Day Network __(35)__ this mission through education, public policy, and\nactivism campaigns.——\"通过教育、公共政策、活动倡议来推行这一使命\"，pursue a\nmission 是\"追求/推行某项使命\"的固定积极搭配，时态、单复数、感情色彩全合。", "points": ["选词填空", "动词"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-36", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 36, "stem": "Hiring managers believe unemployed workers over 45 lack good skills and are less adaptable.", "options": null, "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】技能差+适应力低\n【定位】Hiring managers have a strong perception bias against 45+ job candidates — they believe that\nmembers of this age group have poor skills and low adaptability\n招聘经理对 45 岁以上的求职者抱有强烈的偏见——他们认为这一年龄群体的成员技能差、\n适应力低。\n【改写】lack good skills ↔ poor skills\n反向短语+名词化的同义替换\nless adaptable ↔ low adaptability\n形容词比较级↔抽象名词\n【辨邻】 F 段 F Managers said they worry that older hires will be reluctant to try new\ntechnologies, and will be unable to learn new skills. 只覆盖\"学技能\"一面，未提及\nless adaptable 对应的\"低适应力\"评价，属典型的\"只覆盖局部\"。\nManagers said they worry that older hires will be reluctant to try new technologies, and will be\nunable to learn new skills.", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-37", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 37, "stem": "Switching to a new career is difficult and getting reemployed after a layoff is even tougher.", "options": null, "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】换职业+被裁后再就业\n【定位】Changing careers is hard. Getting back into work after you've been laid off is even harder.\n换工作是难的。被裁员后重新找到工作就更难。\n【改写】Switching to a new career is difficult ↔ Changing careers is hard\n动词与形容词的同义替换\ngetting reemployed after a layoff is even tougher ↔\nGetting back into work after you've been laid off is even harder\n动名词搭配+形容词比较级的同义", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-38", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 38, "stem": "People from poor neighborhoods tend to have the least interest in retraining.", "options": null, "answer": "J", "analysis": "【答案】J 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】穷社区+最不愿再培训\n【定位】The people least interested in retraining are more likely to come from historically\ndisadvantaged communities, more likely to have low incomes, and are more likely to have the\nleast schooling after getting their high-school diploma or earlier.\n对再培训最缺乏兴趣的人更可能来自历史上处境不利的社区，更可能收入低，更可能教育程\n度仅到高中或更低。\n【改写】People from poor neighborhoods ↔ come from historically disadvantaged communities\npoor neighborhoods↔disadvantaged communities 的同义替换\nthe least interest in retraining ↔ The people least interested in retraining\n形容词与名词的形式互换", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-39", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 39, "stem": "Hiring managers who are not yet 45 years old seem unwilling to hire people their senior.", "options": null, "answer": "F", "analysis": "【答案】F 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】未满 45 的招聘经理+不愿招更年长者\n【定位】Besides, the majority of hiring managers are under 45 — and seem reluctant to hire people\nolder than themselves.\n此外，大多数招聘经理本身不满 45 岁——并且似乎不愿意聘用比他们年长的人。\n【改写】Hiring managers who are not yet 45 years old ↔ the majority of hiring managers are under 45\nnot yet 45↔under 45 同义\nunwilling to hire people their senior ↔ seem reluctant to hire people older than themselves\nsenior↔older than themselves 的同义替换\n【辨邻】 D 段 D they still don't want to hire them 讲的是经理对 45+ 求职者的偏见，并未提到\n题干强调的 not yet 45 years old 即经理本身的年龄因素。\nAlthough such managers admit that post-45 hires turn out on average to be just as good as or better\nthan younger workers, they still don't want to hire them.", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-40", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 40, "stem": "Some analysts find age 45+ jobless workers are most likely to be unemployed for more than a year.", "options": null, "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】失业超过一年\n【定位】And if you're out of work past the age of 45, there's nearly a two in three chance you'll be out\nof work for over a year, they find.\n他们发现，如果你过了 45 岁又失业，那么你将有近三分之二的概率失业超过一年。\n【改写】age 45+ jobless workers ↔ if you're out of work past the age of 45\n名词化↔条件从句的等值\nmost likely to be unemployed for more than a year ↔\nthere's nearly a two in three chance you'll be out of work for over a year\n概率短语↔最高级形容词的等值\nSome analysts find ↔ they find\nthey 指代分析师的明确化", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-41", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 41, "stem": "People who had succeeded in career change after 45 told a nonprofit organization they owed a great deal to the education and training they had received.", "options": null, "answer": "I", "analysis": "【答案】I 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】成功转职者+告诉非营利组织+归功培训\n【定位】Those who had successfully changed careers after 45 told Generation that education and\ntraining had been a big help — and that included in-person, on-the-job training, \"informal\nlearning,\" and online courses — with or without certification.\n那些 45 岁后成功转换职业的人告诉 Generation：教育和培训给了他们很大帮助——这些\n培训包括面对面的、在岗培训、\"非正式学习\"以及在线课程——有无证书都算。\n【改写】People who had succeeded in career change after 45 ↔\nThose who had successfully changed careers after 45\n名词短语↔副词+动词的等值\ntold a nonprofit organization ↔ told Generation\n专名↔属性的跨段回溯等值\nthey owed a great deal to the education and training they had received ↔\neducation and training had been a big help\nowed a great deal to↔had been a big help 的同义替换\n【辨邻】 G 段 G Among those over 45 who'd successfully switched careers, 74% said\ntraining helped them get their new job. 只给出比例，未指明对话对象，缺少题干\n强调的\"告诉一个非营利组织\"这一动作。\nAmong those over 45 who'd successfully switched careers, 74% said training helped them get their\nnew job.\nH 段 H Midcareer switchers overwhelmingly say that training enabled them to\nshift to a new career path 是作者对结论的概括式转述，没有题干的\"told a\nnonprofit organization\"动作链条。\nMidcareer switchers overwhelmingly say that training enabled them to shift to a new career path", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-42", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 42, "stem": "Older workers who actively pursue more education and training have a good chance of being hired.", "options": null, "answer": "G", "analysis": "【答案】G 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】积极教育培训+较好录用机会\n【定位】Three-quarters of hiring managers said they'd be more likely to hire an over-45 who had\nrelevant education, training or credentials(文凭).\n四分之三的招聘经理表示，他们更愿意聘用接受过相关教育、培训或拥有相关文凭的 45 岁\n以上者。\n【改写】Older workers who actively pursue more education and training ↔\nOlder workers who've actively engaged in more education and training relevant to their jobs\npursue↔engaged in 同义替换\nhave a good chance of being hired ↔\nThree-quarters of hiring managers said they'd be more likely to hire an over-45 who had\nrelevant education, training or credentials\n高比例+more likely to hire↔a good chance of being hired\n【辨邻】 I 段 I Hiring managers said training was three times more likely to get them to\nhire applicants over age 45 than, say, government subsidies(补贴). 用\"培训 vs 补\n贴\"对比，主语落在\"训练\"而非\"求职者机会\"。\nHiring managers said training was three times more likely to get them to hire applicants over age 45\nthan, say, government subsidies(补贴).", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-43", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 43, "stem": "A new study finds that more education and training helps midcareer individuals find a new job.", "options": null, "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】一项新研究+教育培训助力中年人找工作\n【定位】But the one thing that can really make a difference? More education and training.\nThese are the results from a new study by Generation, a nonprofit founded by former\nMcKinsey consultants.\n但真正能起作用的是什么呢？更多的教育和培训。这是来自 Generation——一家由前麦肯\n锡顾问创立的非营利组织——的一项新研究的结果。\n【改写】A new study finds that more education and training helps midcareer individuals find a new job ↔\nMore education and training. These are the results from a new study by Generation\nfindings↔results from 的等值\nmidcareer individuals find a new job ↔ midcareer employment\n中年人就业话题的同义指代\n【辨邻】 G 段 G Three-quarters of hiring managers said they'd be more likely to hire an\nover-45 who had relevant education 用具体比例展开研究结论，并未用\"A new\nstudy\"这种结论引子词。\nThree-quarters of hiring managers said they'd be more likely to hire an over-45 who had relevant\neducation, training or credentials(文凭).", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-44", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 44, "stem": "Owing to the internet, it is now more convenient than ever to receive training in new skills.", "options": null, "answer": "L", "analysis": "【答案】L 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】互联网+训练新技能从未如此便捷\n【定位】And it has never been easier or cheaper to gain instruction in new skills, thanks to\nthe internet.\n多亏了互联网，学习新技能从未如此容易或便宜。\n【改写】Owing to the internet ↔ thanks to the internet\nOwing to↔thanks to 同义介词短语\nmore convenient than ever ↔ has never been easier or cheaper\nnever+比较级↔more 比较级 than ever 等值\nreceive training in new skills ↔ gain instruction in new skills\nreceive↔gain；training↔instruction 的同义替换\n【辨邻】 I 段 I education and training had been a big help — and that included in-person,\non-the-job training, \"informal learning,\" and online courses 列举了培训方式，但\nOwing to the internet 这一核心锚点在 I 段缺席。\neducation and training had been a big help — and that included in-person, on-the-job training,\n\"informal learning,\" and online courses — with or without certification.", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-m-45", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 45, "stem": "People over 45 stimulated by training suffer shorter periods of unemployment, get more job offers and have greater satisfaction in them.", "options": null, "answer": "H", "analysis": "【答案】H 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】受培训刺激者+三项收益\n【定位】And when they asked over-45 candidates about their attitudes, they found that \"those who are\nexcited by training are unemployed for less time, receive more job offers, and are more\nsatisfied by the job offers they receive.\"\n当他们询问 45 岁以上候选人的态度时，发现\"那些因培训而兴奋的人失业时间更短、获得更\n多录用、对所收到的录用更满意\"。\n【改写】People over 45 stimulated by training ↔ those who are excited by training\nstimulated↔excited 同义形容词\nsuffer shorter periods of unemployment ↔ are unemployed for less time\nshorter periods of unemployment↔unemployed for less time 等值\nget more job offers ↔ receive more job offers\nget↔receive 同义动词\nhave greater satisfaction in them ↔ are more satisfied by the job offers they receive\n名词化↔形容词的等值\n【辨邻】 G 段 G Three-quarters of hiring managers said they'd be more likely to hire an\nover-45 who had relevant education, training or credentials 只覆盖\"更易被录\n用\"，没有题干的\"失业时间更短+offer 更多+满意度更高\"三项收益。\nThree-quarters of hiring managers said they'd be more likely to hire an over-45 who had relevant\neducation, training or credentials(文凭). Among those over 45 who'd successfully switched careers,\n74% said training helped them get their new job.", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-46", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 46, "stem": "What do we learn about New York's Eleven Madison Park?", "options": ["A) It is the first vegan restaurant to receive the highest Michelin rating.", "B) It is the first restaurant in the city to remove meat from its menu.", "C) It was famed throughout the U.S. for its fancy regional dishes.", "D) It was established as a three-star Michelin restaurant in 2011."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题）\n【判型】What do we learn about New York's Eleven Madison Park? 问的是关于某对象的客观信\n息，没有 infer/imply 等推断信号，属典型细节题。\n【拆句】What do we learn about New York's Eleven Madison Park? 是一句结构平铺直叙的特殊\n疑问句，learn about 后跟宾语，无陷阱。\n【定位】New York's Eleven Madison Park has become the first vegan(素⻝主义的) restaurant to be\nawarded three Michelin stars.\n纽约的 Eleven Madison Park 成为首家获颁米其林三星的素食餐厅。\n【选项】A) ✓ 正确\nthe first vegan(素⻝主义的) restaurant to be awarded three Michelin stars ↔\nthe first vegan restaurant to receive the highest Michelin rating\nIt is the first vegan restaurant to receive the highest Michelin rating. 完整覆盖了预\n判的三要素，首家、素食、最高评级，且无任何额外信息，与定位句一一对应。\nB) 偷换概念\n原文说的是首家获三星的素食餐厅，the first restaurant in the city to remove meat\nfrom its menu 把首家偷换到了全市首家撤肉上，原文并无此说。\nC) 无中生有\n原文 famed for its fancy animal-based dishes 说的是过去以荤菜闻名，famed\nthroughout the U.S. for its fancy regional dishes 一改 animal-based 为 regional\n（地方菜），二加范围 throughout the U.S.（全美），都无原文支持。\nD) 偷换概念\n原文 received its first three-star Michelin rating in 2011 说的是 2011 年首次获三\n星，established as a three-star Michelin restaurant in 2011 把获评偷换成建立，与\n原文 its nearly 25-year history 也矛盾。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-47", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 47, "stem": "Why did Daniel Humm decide to remove meat from the menu of his restaurant?", "options": ["A) To encourage more customers to be vegan.", "B) To contribute to a sustainable food system.", "C) To show the appeal of a plant-based menu.", "D) To strive for the three-star Michelin rating."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题）\n【判型】Why did Daniel Humm decide to remove meat from the menu of his restaurant? 用\nWhy 直接问原因，对应原文必有显性的原因表述。\n【拆句】Why did Daniel Humm decide to remove meat from the menu of his restaurant? 主\n干为 Why did X decide to do Y，decide to 后接动作，无修饰陷阱。\n【定位】However, last year, the restaurant's co-owner and famous chef, Daniel Humm, made the bold\ndecision to remove meat from the menu, citing our unsustainable food system.\n然而，去年餐厅的联合所有者兼名厨 Daniel Humm 做出了大胆决定，将肉从菜单中撤下，\n理由是我们的食物体系不可持续。\n【选项】A) 偷换概念\nTo encourage more customers to be vegan. 把动机应对不可持续体系偷换成鼓励顾\n客吃素，原文 Humm 的关注点是体系层面而非顾客饮食选择。\nB) ✓ 正确\nciting our unsustainable food system ↔ To contribute to a sustainable food system.\n四个选项中只有 To contribute to a sustainable food system. 含 sustainable 这个原\n文核心词根，且其表达的目的与 citing 的事实方向自洽。\nC) 答非所问\nIf we can show the possibilities of eating plant-based food in this setting, it can\nopen a lot of doors 是 Humm 对该决定后续效果的展望，而非他做决定的原因，时间\n和因果关系都被改写。\nD) 与原文相反\n三星米其林是撤肉之后才获得的结果，To strive for the three-star Michelin rating. 把\n它说成做决定的目的，因果关系与原文相反。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-48", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 48, "stem": "What did Daniel Humm think of his move to a meat-free menu?", "options": ["A) It was a worthwhile effort even though he was unsure of its success.", "B) It would set a model for many more restaurants to follow.", "C) It was a mad gamble few chefs in the fine dining world would risk taking.", "D) It would prove a right step to take in today's catering business."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题）\n【判型】What did Daniel Humm think of his move to a meat-free menu? 问的是 Humm 自己\n怎么看，原文必有他直接表态的引语。\n【拆句】What did Daniel Humm think of his move to a meat-free menu? think of 是固定搭\n配，意为对...的看法，主干清晰，无陷阱。\n【定位】At the time, Humm acknowledged the move was risky, admitting that \"it wasn't clear if guests\nwould come\", but called the gamble \"a risk worth taking.\"\n当时 Humm 承认此举有风险，承认不清楚客人是否还会来，但他把这场赌博称作一次值得\n冒的险。\n【选项】A) ✓ 正确\nit wasn't clear if guests would come ↔ he was unsure of its success\na risk worth taking ↔ a worthwhile effort\nIt was a worthwhile effort even though he was unsure of its success. 用 even\nthough 把值得与不确定连起来，恰好对应原文 but 引出的双面态度。\nB) 答非所问\nIt would set a model for many more restaurants to follow. 是 Humm 在 it can\nopen a lot of doors 中说的对外效用，而非他对自己这一举动的内心评价。\nC) 过度推断\na mad gamble few chefs in the fine dining world would risk taking 用 mad、few\nchefs would risk 把原文的 risky 与 a risk worth taking 夸大成几乎没人敢冒的疯狂赌\n博，原文 Humm 并未做此横向比较。\nD) 偷换概念\nIt would prove a right step to take in today's catering business. 把 Humm 对自己\n这一步的个人评价换成对整个餐饮业的判断，且 a right step 也比 a risk worth taking\n多了行业普遍正确的隐含。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-49", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 49, "stem": "What does Michelin's 2022 New York guide say about Eleven Madison Park's decision?", "options": ["A) It elevates the restaurant's cooking to an art form.", "B) It proves the validity of ratings awarded by Michelin.", "C) It shows a daring foresight regarding future fine dining.", "D) It is an effort to transform the restaurant into a luxury one."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题）\n【判型】What does Michelin's 2022 New York guide say about Eleven Madison Park's\ndecision? 问指南说了什么，对应原文必有指南的引语或转述。\n【拆句】What does Michelin's 2022 New York guide say about Eleven Madison Park's\ndecision? say about 后接讨论对象，结构线性、无陷阱。\n【定位】Now, this impressive new accomplishment validates Eleven Madison Park's decision to take\nmeat off the menu and embrace plant-based foods, with Michelin's 2022 New York guide\nbranding it 'a bold vision of luxury dining'.\n如今，这一令人瞩目的新成就印证了 Eleven Madison Park 撤肉、拥抱植物饮食的决定；\n米其林 2022 纽约指南将其誉为奢华餐饮的大胆愿景。\n【选项】A) 张冠李戴\nIt elevates the restaurant's cooking to an art form. 取自 Their cooking is elevated\nto an art form，而那是米其林对三星厨师的总体描述，不是 2022 纽约指南对 Eleven\nMadison Park 这个决定的表态。\nB) 与原文相反\nIt proves the validity of ratings awarded by Michelin. 把指南怎么说决定颠倒为决定\n证明了米其林评级的有效性，原文 validates 的对象是 decision，而不是评级。\nC) ✓ 正确\na bold vision of luxury dining ↔ a daring foresight regarding future fine dining\nIt shows a daring foresight regarding future fine dining. 同时给出大胆远见与高\n端、未来餐饮两个要素，且整体语气与原文引号短语一致。\nD) 无中生有\nIt is an effort to transform the restaurant into a luxury one. 把指南的评价改成餐厅\n的主观努力（an effort to），且新增把餐厅变成奢华餐厅这一目的，原文从未提及。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-50", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 50, "stem": "What does the awarding of three Michelin stars to Eleven Madison Park indicate?", "options": ["A) An optimistic vision of vegan foods becoming mainstream.", "B) A greater responsibility for the culinary world to undertake.", "C) A strong incentive for more restaurants to offer healthier foods to their customers.", "D) An explicit recognition of the rising importance of restaurants serving vegan foods."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （推断题）\n【判型】What does the awarding of three Michelin stars to Eleven Madison Park indicate? 中\n的 indicate 是推断题专属信号词。\n【拆句】What does the awarding of three Michelin stars to Eleven Madison Park indicate? 主\n干为 What does X indicate，X 是动名词短语 the awarding of...，结构清晰、无陷阱。\n【定位】\"Their cooking is elevated to an art form and some of their dishes are destined to become\nclassics,\" reads Michelin's website, in a clear nod to plant-based foods' growing significance\nin the culinary(烹饪的) world.\n米其林官网写道：他们的烹饪被提升为一种艺术形式，他们的部分菜肴注定将成为经典；这\n是对植物饮食在烹饪界日益增长的重要性的明确认可。\n【选项】A) 过度推断\nAn optimistic vision of vegan foods becoming mainstream. 把地位上升（rising\nimportance）推到成为主流（becoming mainstream），且加上乐观愿景，跨度超过\n原文一步可达的范围。\nB) 答非所问\nA greater responsibility for the culinary world to undertake. 取自 luxury\ncompanies have a real role to play and a responsibility 这种 Humm 的呼吁，而非\n授星事件本身所表明的含义。\nC) 偷换概念\nA strong incentive for more restaurants to offer healthier foods to their\ncustomers. 一把素食或植物偷换成更健康的食物（healthier foods），二把地位上升变\n成激励更多餐厅，原文从未谈健康层面，也未谈对其他餐厅的激励效应。\nD) ✓ 正确\nin a clear nod to plant-based foods' growing significance in the culinary(烹饪的) world ↔\nAn explicit recognition of the rising importance of restaurants serving vegan foods.\nAn explicit recognition of the rising importance of restaurants serving vegan\nfoods. 仅把植物饮食地位上升在表达载体上落到提供素食的餐厅，恰是从授星事件能合\n理外推的一步，无超过原文的判断。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "推断题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-51", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 51, "stem": "What does the passage say is of importance regarding genetic tests?", "options": ["A) Knowing their accuracy.", "B) Evaluating their applicability.", "C) Utilizing the information they provide.", "D) Weighing the consequences they have."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题）\n【判型】What does the passage say is of importance regarding genetic tests 直接问文章\"说了\n什么\"，没有 infer/imply 这种推断信号词，是查找型细节题。\n【拆句】What does the passage say is of importance regarding genetic tests 主干是 \"What\ndoes the passage say\"，宾语从句省略了 that，完整化即 \"the passage say (that) ... is of\nimportance\"，regarding genetic tests 是介词短语作话题限定，相当于 about。无陷阱。\n【定位】Whether you are taking a DNA test to build your extended DNA family tree, or want precise\ninformation on inborn health conditions, it is important to understand how accurate genetic\ntests are, and what information we can rely upon.\n无论你是为了构建延伸的 DNA 家谱树而做基因测试，还是想获得关于先天健康状况的精确\n信息，搞清楚基因检测到底有多准、我们可以依赖哪些信息，都是很重要的。\n【选项】A) ✓ 正确\nit is important to understand how accurate genetic tests are ↔ Knowing their accuracy\n预判说\"知道它准不准\"，Knowing their accuracy 一字不差地说\"知道它的准确度\"，直\n接锁定 A。\nB) 无中生有\nEvaluating their applicability 中的 applicability（适用性/可用性）在 P1 里完全没\n提，作者只强调准确度。\nC) 偷换概念\nwhat information we can rely upon 说的是\"哪些信息可以依赖\"——是判断可不可\n信，而不是 Utilizing the information they provide 说的\"利用它给出的信息\"。\nD) 无中生有\nWeighing the consequences they have 里的 consequences（后果）在原文里没有任\n何对应——作者通篇只在谈准确度，没谈\"后果\"。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-52", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 52, "stem": "What kind of genetic tests tend to be comparatively reliable?", "options": ["A) Those complex enough to reveal the genetics behind a trait.", "B) Those looking for traits responsible for certain diseases.", "C) Those focusing on the specific questions being asked.", "D) Those looking for traits determined by a single gene."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题）\n【判型】What kind of genetic tests tend to be comparatively reliable 是查询事实性比较，找到\n原文那句 \"X 更可靠\" 即可对答案。\n【拆句】What kind of genetic tests tend to be comparatively reliable 中 \"tend to be\" 是\"倾向\n于、往往是\"的弱化系动词结构，相当于 are usually；comparatively 修饰 reliable，是\"相\n对来说\"，并非\"绝对可靠\"。\n【定位】For example, tests for traits that depend on a single gene provide much more reliable results,\nbecause you can see whether a disease-causing trait is present.\n举个例子，对于那些只依赖单个基因的性状，相关检测能给出准确得多的结果，因为你可以\n直接看到致病性状到底存不存在。\n【选项】A) 与原文相反\nThose complex enough to reveal the genetics behind a trait 说\"复杂到能揭示性状\n背后基因\"，原文却是\"取决于单基因的简单情况更可靠\"，方向相反。\nB) 偷换概念\nThose looking for traits responsible for certain diseases 抓住的是 a disease-\ncausing trait——但原文里 \"致病性状\" 只是\"为什么单基因检测可靠\"的解释，不是\"哪\n一类检测可靠\"。\nC) 偷换概念\nThose focusing on the specific questions being asked 把 the specific question\nyou ask 直接搬来，但原文那一句讲的是\"准确度取决于问题\"，不是\"针对特定问题的检\n测更可靠\"。\nD) ✓ 正确\ntests for traits that depend on a single gene ↔\nThose looking for traits determined by a single gene\n全篇只有 single gene 这一处出现\"单基因\"，且就配着 more reliable，预判和 D 完全\n对齐，锁定 D。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-53", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 53, "stem": "What do we learn about genetic health tests from the passage?", "options": ["A) They are unable to identify certain hereditary diseases by themselves.", "B) They are generally unable to separate genetic and non-genetic factors.", "C) They cannot independently identify the majority of potential diseases.", "D) They cannot tell apart the impact of lifestyle and that of the environment."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题）\n【判型】What do we learn about genetic health tests from the passage 问的是文章\"告诉我们\n什么\"，属于事实查询，不是推断。\n【拆句】What do we learn about genetic health tests from the passage 句式为 \"learn about X\nfrom Y\"——从 Y 中了解到关于 X 的什么；about 后是话题，from 后是来源。结构平铺直\n叙，无陷阱。\n【定位】While certain rare diseases can be easily identified, most potential health conditions cannot be\nidentified by genetic testing alone.\n虽然某些罕见疾病能轻松识别出来，但大多数潜在的健康问题靠基因检测一项是查不出\n来的。\n【选项】A) 与原文相反\nThey are unable to identify certain hereditary diseases by themselves 用 certain\n（某些）替换原文的 most（多数）——原文恰恰说 certain rare diseases can be\neasily identified，让步从句中的 certain rare 反而是\"能识别的\"，A 把它颠倒了。\nB) 无中生有\nThey are generally unable to separate genetic and non-genetic factors 凭空加\n了\"区分基因与非基因因素\"这件事——原文只说健康状况受非基因因素影响，从未要求\n基因检测\"区分\"两者。\nC) ✓ 正确\nmost potential health conditions cannot be identified by genetic testing alone ↔\nThey cannot independently identify the majority of potential diseases\npredict 关键的\"多数\"\"靠它单独\"两个限定词，C 选项用 the majority of 和\nindependently 一一对应，且主语\"基因健康检测\"一致，无任何过度信息。\nD) 偷换概念\nThey cannot tell apart the impact of lifestyle and that of the environment 把\nlifestyle 和 environment 单挑出来谈区分，但原文这两词只是 non-genetic factors,\nsuch as lifestyle, the environment, and many others 的举例，且 also 之后从未谈\"区\n分两者影响\"。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-54", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 54, "stem": "What makes genetic tests for multi-factorial traits tricky to interpret?", "options": ["A) The challenge in determining the role of each individual gene.", "B) The difficulty of foretelling how the various genes will interact.", "C) The difficulty of telling genetic factors from environmental ones.", "D) The enormous work to identify the hundreds of genes involved."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题）\n【判型】What makes genetic tests for multi-factorial traits tricky to interpret 是 What makes\nX Y 的句式，问的是事实层面的原因，原文里有现成原因句。\n【拆句】What makes genetic tests for multi-factorial traits tricky to interpret 结构是 \"make +\n宾语 + 形容词\"——\"使...变得难以解读\"。What 作主语，问的是导致这件难事的原因；to\ninterpret 是后置不定式作形容词补足语。\n【定位】A test can look at many genes at once, but it's difficult to predict how they will play together.\n一次基因检测可以同时查看许多基因，但很难预测这些基因放在一起会怎么\"协作\"。\n【选项】A) 偷换概念\nThe challenge in determining the role of each individual gene 把\"每个单基因的作\n用\"塞进答案，但 each contributing a little to the outcome 只是顺带一提\"每个贡献\n一点\"，原文并没有说\"难以确定每个基因的作用\"。\nB) ✓ 正确\nit's difficult to predict how they will play together ↔\nThe difficulty of foretelling how the various genes will interact\n整篇文章只有 P6 这一句用了 difficult to predict 的结构，预判\"基因互动难以预测\"严\n丝合缝地对应 B 选项的\"预测基因如何相互作用的难度\"，直接锁定。\nC) 无中生有\nThe difficulty of telling genetic factors from environmental ones 编出\"区分基因\n因素与环境因素\"这件事——原文只说\"还要把非基因因素也考虑进去\"，从未要求\"区分\n两者\"。\nD) 无中生有\nThe enormous work to identify the hundreds of genes involved 把焦点放到\"识别\n这几百个基因的庞大工作量\"——原文 hundreds of genes 只是说数量大，没说\"识别它\n们工作量巨大\"，也根本没说\"工作量\"才是\"难解读\"的原因。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2025-12-3-r-55", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 55, "stem": "What does the passage say about DNA tests to predict personality or talents?", "options": ["A) They are solid scientific bases for application.", "B) They are helpful in finding a romantic match.", "C) They do not look promising at the moment.", "D) They do not make any sense at present."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （态度题）\n【判型】What does the passage say about DNA tests to predict personality or talents——配\n合选项里 do not look promising、do not make any sense 这种全是态度评价的格局，本\n质是问作者对这件事的态度。\n【拆句】What does the passage say about DNA tests to predict personality or talents 中\n\"DNA tests to predict ...\" 的不定式 to predict 作 DNA tests 的后置定语，等于 \"DNA\ntests that predict ...\"——\"用来预测人格或才能的 DNA 测试\"。\n【定位】Tests that offer to find your perfect romantic match and those claiming to predict personality\nor talents based on your DNA are pure nonsense. At the moment, the scientific bases for these\napplications are non-existent or incredibly weak.\n那些声称能帮你找到完美恋爱对象的检测、以及那些号称能根据 DNA 预测性格或才能的检\n测，都是纯粹的胡说八道。眼下，这些应用的科学依据要么压根不存在，要么薄弱得离谱。\n【选项】A) 与原文相反\nThey are solid scientific bases for application 说\"是坚实的科学依据\"，原文恰好说\nthe scientific bases for these applications are non-existent or incredibly weak\n——科学依据要么不存在要么极弱，方向完全相反。\nB) 与原文相反\nThey are helpful in finding a romantic match 抓了原文里的另一个例子 find your\nperfect romantic match——但原文是把它当作\"也是胡说\"的反面例子，B 却说它\"有帮\n助\"，立场反了。\nC) 偷换概念\nThey do not look promising at the moment 译过来是\"目前看起来不太有前景\"——\n但原文是 pure nonsense（纯属胡扯），属于强烈否定，C 把它弱化成\"前景不佳\"这种\n中性偏负的客气说法。\nD) ✓ 正确\nare pure nonsense ↔ They do not make any sense at present\nAt the moment ↔ at present\n预判\"作者强烈否定\"对应 do not make any sense；at present 又把 at the moment\n这个时间限定带上了——D 一字不漏地把作者的核心态度搬过来了。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "态度题"]}], "listeningSharedWith": "2025-12-1"});
